   "unmapped": [
    "Reward is observed by a memoryless client which must encode it with second moment at most P; the encoded value is sent over an AWGN channel with noise variance sigma^2, and the learner only sees the channel output (SNR = P/sigma^2)",
    "Learner may send side information to the client each round and chooses encoder/decoder",
    "Rewards centred are 1-subgaussian and have second moment E[X^2] <= B_rew^2 with B_rew >= 1",
    "The learner knows SNR (P, sigma^2) and B_rew"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "the client encodes this reward using an encoding function $ C_t \\colon \\R \\times \\mathcal{S}  \\to \\R$ ... must satisfy the power constraint $\\E{C_t(X_{t, A_t}, S_t)^2} \\leq P$ ... $Y_t = C_t(X_{t, A_t}, S_t) + Z_t$ ... We assume that $X_{1, i}-\\mu_i$ is subgaussian with variance factor $1$ ... $\\E{X_{1, i}^2} \\leq B^2.$"
  }
